<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Frentani</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 304 BCE (approx.) · capital Larinum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Oscan-speaking people of the central Adriatic coast, related to the Samnites, who became allies of Rome in 304 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Frentani occupied the coastal hills of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molise">Molise</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abruzzo">Abruzzo</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangro">Sangro</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fortore">Fortore</a> rivers. Ancient writers considered them of Samnite stock, and they spoke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscan-language">Oscan</a>. Their history before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> is known only from scattered references.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their main centres included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasto">Histonium</a> (Vasto), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lanciano">Anxanum</a> (Lanciano) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/larino">Larinum</a>, which some writers treated as a separate people. They farmed, herded and traded along the coast. They usually kept apart from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/samnite-league">Samnite League</a> and its wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Frentani made an alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 304 BCE, at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-samnite-war">Second Samnite War</a>, and fought for Rome against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>. They joined the Italian rebels in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a> of 91–88 BCE, then received citizenship and were absorbed into Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/frentani.jpg" alt="Frentani" width="320" height="286"><figcaption>Image: William Robert Shepherd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Frentani.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 304 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Larinum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Oscan polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oscan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-452&amp;focus=frentani" aria-label="Frentani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5043 689 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Frentani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5363 945L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5363 945h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5363 945h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Larinum. <a href="/atlas?year=-452&amp;focus=frentani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

